                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_42">Beauly,
                        Inverness-shire. Priory of St Mary the Virgin and St John the Baptist of the
                        order of Vallis Caulium</orgName><p>At end, in a difficult hand, 'Iste
                        est(?) liber ut(?) pertinet priori nicholai barchan' cum suis monachis de
                        monasterio belli loci quod [....] in tempore predicti prioris [.....]
                        ordinauit quod numquam fuesset in suis maioribus matutinis cantator' cum
                        messis ac vesperis [....] ut exorat [....] queso ut mors predicti prioris
                        non sit statim. Per me dauidum barchan scriptum anno domini mo quingentesimo
                        xxjo'.</p><p>E. C. Batten, The Charters of the Priory of Beauly (London
                        1877), gives the prior's name in 1525 as Nicholas without
                     surname.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">On cover: 'Ex dono vicecomitis de Tarbert
                     1686'.</provenance>
